.TH CREATE-CLASTER-DEB.SH 1 "2026-09-12" "pg_claster_creator 2.4.0" "Developer Commands"
.SH NAME
create-claster-deb.sh \- build claster-creator Debian packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B create-claster-deb.sh
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B create-claster-deb.sh
builds installable Debian packages from the project source tree. It creates a
fresh filesystem skeleton below
.IR tmp/create-claster-deb.XXXXXX/rootFs ,
populates it, builds the package, and removes the temporary tree on exit.
The tmp parent is removed only if created by this run and empty after cleanup.
Pre-existing directories and unrelated files are preserved, also on failure.
Packages are written to
.I dist
unless another output directory is selected.
.PP
Both control and data archives use gzip explicitly, including fakeroot builds,
so packages remain readable by older Astra Linux 1.6/1.7 dpkg versions.
.PP
With no arguments, an interactive mode menu is shown. Modes 2 through 4 are
interactive by default; use
.B --non-interactive
for automation. Every package depends on
.BR postgresql-common .
.PP
In the interactive backup list for modes 3 and 4, each archive type is followed
by its aligned file size. The value uses two fractional digits, a two-letter
unit, and no more than nine characters. The size is obtained with
.BR stat (1)
without opening or extracting the archive.
.SH MODES
.PP
Interactive steps clear the terminal. Submenus offer 0 to go back; invalid input
returns to the previous step. Invalid main-menu input exits. Enter accepts a
displayed default; EOF cancels the wizard without building a package.
.TP
.B 1
Install management and scheduled-backup scripts, configuration, documentation,
manual pages, and command symlinks.
.TP
.B 2
Install the files and create an empty PostgreSQL cluster.
.TP
.B 3
Install the files and restore a cluster from an embedded cold backup.
.TP
.B 4
Install the files, create a cluster, and restore an embedded hot database dump.
.PP
For modes 2 through 4, postinst first checks the exact cluster version and name.
If an unrelated cluster is already registered, postinst prints a warning, skips
the remaining deployment actions, and exits with status 0. Completion markers
are honored only while the target cluster is registered. If it was removed,
stale completion and intermediate markers are cleared and deployment runs again.
An interrupted plan with a registered cluster and an intermediate marker resumes
the pending restore or data-movement step. A final marker is never created until
the target cluster has been verified.
.PP
When an occupied requested port is replaced during mode 2 or mode 4 cluster
creation, postinst repeats the warning after all actions, including hot restore.
The final notice shows the actual port and a
.B create-claster.sh --action port
command for changing it later.
.SH POSTGRES PRO VERSION SELECTION
In mode 4 with
.B postgrespro-ent
and no explicit
.BR --package ,
the value of
.B --pg-version
is the minimum target major version. Package dependencies list PostgreSQL Pro
contrib 18, 17, and so on down to that minimum, with newer alternatives first.
Each contrib package has an exact dependency on the server of the same release,
so APT selects a matching server and extension set. The generated postinst uses
the release that was actually installed for cluster creation and hot restore.
An already installed minimum release is retained.
.PP
For example, a mode 4 package built with a minimum of 14 installs PostgreSQL
Pro 16 when the target repository offers releases 13 through 16. Release 13 is
not an eligible alternative.
.PP
Install the resulting local package with
.B apt install ./PACKAGE.deb
to resolve alternatives and download missing dependencies. The
.B dpkg -i
command alone does not download server packages; it requires a subsequent
.B apt -f install
when dependencies are missing.
.PP
An explicit
.B --package
disables this policy and keeps an exact dependency. Mode 3 cold restore always
uses the exact physical-backup version: its package depends on
.B postgresql-common
and the exact server package recorded in backup metadata, without an
automatically added contrib package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print complete usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Print the builder version and exit.
.TP
.BI "-m, --mode " MODE
Select mode 1, 2, 3, or 4.
.TP
.BI "--pg-family " FAMILY
Select postgresql, postgrespro-ent, tantor-free, tantor-se (Special Edition), or tantor-be (Basic Edition).
.TP
.BI "--pg-version " VERSION
Set the PostgreSQL major version. For automatic PostgreSQL Pro mode 4 packages,
this is the minimum target version.
.TP
.BI "--cluster-name " NAME
Set the target cluster name.
.TP
.BI "--port " PORT
Set the target TCP port.
.TP
.BI "--package " PACKAGE
Set an exact server package and dependency, disabling automatic selection of a
newer PostgreSQL Pro release.
.TP
.BI "--schema " NAME
Set the schema and owner role for a new cluster.
.TP
.BI "--user " NAME
Set the application login role.
.TP
.BI "--password " PASSWORD
Set the password stored in the protected deployment plan.
.TP
.BI "--data-root " DIRECTORY
Set a custom cluster data root. The package creates it during deployment when
it does not exist.
.TP
.BI "--backup-file " FILE
Select a cold backup for mode 3 or a hot backup for mode 4.
.TP
.BI "--backup-dir " DIRECTORY
Select the directory used by interactive backup selection.
.TP
.BI "--database " NAME
Set the target database for mode 4.
.TP
.BI "--depends " PACKAGES
Add comma-separated Debian package dependencies. The option may be repeated and
is accepted only in modes 2 through 4. With automatic PostgreSQL Pro selection,
server packages already covered by eligible contrib alternatives are omitted.
.TP
.BI "--output-dir " DIRECTORY
Select the package destination. The default is
.IR dist .
.TP
.BR -i , " --interactive"
Explicitly enable the mode 2 through 4 configuration dialog.
.TP
.BR -n , " --non-interactive"
Disable prompts and require complete arguments.
.TP
.BR -f , " --force"
Replace an existing output package.
.SH REPEAT LAST INTERACTIVE BUILD
After an interactive build is confirmed, the builder atomically writes
.I create-claster-deb-last.sh
next to itself. If that directory is not writable, it uses
.IR ~/tmp/create-claster-deb-last.sh
and creates
.I ~/tmp
when necessary.
The file has mode 0755 and contains a complete command with
.BR --non-interactive ,
absolute paths, and
.BR --force .
The resulting mode is verified and a warning is printed when the filesystem
does not preserve POSIX permissions.
Running it repeats the last interactive build without prompts. A builder run
with
.B --non-interactive
does not create or change this file. Mode 2 and mode 4 commands contain the
configured database password, so access to the home directory must be restricted.
.SH PACKAGE INSTALLATION ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLASTER_FORCE_INSTALL=1
For modes 2 through 4, ignore previous completion markers, remove an existing
target cluster without creating a backup, verify its removal, and execute the
complete package plan again. This is the force option used for a mode 3 cold
restore.
.TP
.B CLASTER_FORCE_DB_INSTALL=1
Mode 4 only. Keep the existing cluster and restore the target database again
from the embedded hot dump with overwrite enabled. If the cluster does not
exist, it is created normally. This flag is rejected for modes 2 and 3.
.PP
The two force variables are mutually exclusive. Set them in the environment of
.BR dpkg (1),
for example:
.PP
.nf
CLASTER_FORCE_INSTALL=1 dpkg -i PACKAGE.deb
CLASTER_FORCE_DB_INSTALL=1 dpkg -i PACKAGE.deb
.fi
.SH PACKAGE NAMES
.nf
claster-creator-VERSION.deb
claster-creator-VERSION-PG-PGVER-CLUSTER-empty.deb
claster-creator-VERSION-PG-PGVER-CLUSTER-full.deb
claster-creator-VERSION-PG-PGVER-CLUSTER-DATABASE.deb
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/pg_claster_creator/TEST-2.1.2-journal-passed.md
Required validation journal, installed by every package mode with permissions 0644.
Release 2.3.2 groups rename, port and data-location actions under the Edit menu.
The bundled 2.1.2 journal is historical and does not validate these new features.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/pg_claster_creator/create-claster-deb.sh
Installed builder. No command symlink is created in
.IR /usr/local/bin .
.TP
.I .new-claster.config
Interactive defaults. Prefer:
.br
.I /usr/local/shared/pg_claster_creator/.new-claster.config
.br
only if absent, use the file beside the resolved script.
.TP
.I create-claster-deb-last.sh
Executable command for repeating the last confirmed interactive build, stored
next to the builder or below
.I ~/tmp
when the builder directory is not writable.
.TP
.I tmp/create-claster-deb.XXXXXX/rootFs
Temporary package filesystem skeleton.
.TP
.I dist
Default output directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&./create-claster-deb.sh
\&./create-claster-deb.sh --mode 1
\&./create-claster-deb.sh --mode 2 --depends postgis,pgbouncer
\&./create-claster-deb.sh --mode 3 --backup-dir /.postgres/backup
\&./create-claster-deb.sh --mode 4 --non-interactive \
  --pg-family postgrespro-ent --pg-version 16 \
  --cluster-name subsys --database asvd \
  --backup-file /.postgres/backup/16-asvd-20260905-105802-dmp.tar.gz
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR create-claster.sh (1),
.BR create-claster-backup.sh (1),
.BR dpkg-deb (1)
